The standard Q-learning objective based on the Bellman equation is to minimize the following loss function:
$
\mathcal{L}_{base}(\theta) = \mathbb{E}_{(s,a,r,s') \sim \mathcal{D}} \left[ \left( Q_\theta(s,a) - \left( r + \gamma \max_{a'} Q_{\theta}(s',a') \right) \right)^2 \right]
