The gradient of $\mathcal{L}_{\text{c}}$ is equal to the gradient of $\frac{ w_{c} }{| \mathcal{X}_{\text{safe}}|} \sum_{x \in \mathcal{X}_{\text{safe}}} \left[\tau \ln\left(\sum_{v \in V_x} \exp \left(\frac{B_\phi(x'_v)}{\tau}\right)\right ) - B_\phi(x')\right]$,  but
with the second term, $B_\phi(x')$, detached from the computational graph during training in Pytorch using the \texttt{tensor.detach()} method. The latter is similar to the loss used in conservative Q learning (CQL)~\citep{kumar2020conservative}, where the Q-function is replaced by $B_\phi$, but CQL does not detach the second term.  
