We want the CCBF values at InD states to be determined mainly by the loss terms $\mathcal{L}_{\text{safe}}$, $\mathcal{L}_{\text{unsafe}}$, $\mathcal{L}_{\text{ascent}}$, $\mathcal{L}_{\text{descent}}$, and $\mathcal{L}_{\text{lip}}$, which enforce the conditions required by the learned CBF to be a valid CBF, while minimally being affected by the conservative loss term $L_c$. We did an ablation study where we did not detach $B_\phi(x')$. Its results, shown in Appendix \ref{app:Lc_detach}, support our argument that that the learned CCBFs without detaching $B_\phi(x')$ generally under-perform those obtained by detaching it. Results of the latter are shown in Section \ref{sec:results}.

