 \subsubsection{Implementation and experimental details}\label{app:swimmer_hopper_implementation_details}
 We first train a dynamics model as described in Section \ref{sec:learn_latent_dynamics}, but instead of employing an autoencoder as in the vision-based task to map observations to latent states, we learn the dynamics directly in safety gymnasium’s native state space. Then, we train the CCBF as described in Section \ref{sec:learn_cbf}, but do not include $\mathcal{L}_{\text{descent}}$. We train the nominal controllers using the offline RL algorithms (COptiDICE \citep{lee2022coptidice}, BEAR-L \citep{xu2022constraints,kumar2019stabilizing}, BCQ-L \citep{xu2022constraints,fujimoto2019off}) and using BC variants as implemented in DSRL~\citep{dsrl}. 
 During evaluation, if the QP was infeasible, we select the closest point in \(\mathcal{U}\) to the constraint boundary. 


\subsubsection{Normalized reward and normalized cost metrics in the safety gymnasium tasks}\label{app:normalizd_metrics}

