So far, we made no assumptions regarding multipartite structure (i.e., only a single variable can change at a time). However, as we show in \emph{End Matter}, for multipartite dynamics and multipartite observables, Eq.~\eqref{eq:dual} can be split into $N$ separate optimization problems, each one involving only a proportional fraction of the variables and observations.
