\PRLsection{Multidimensional TUR~\eqref{eq:GturDef}}
For a stationary system without odd variables,  $\tilde{p}(\traj)=p(\revtraj)$, letting us write the EP as
\begin{align*}
\ep=\sum_{\traj} p(\traj)\ln \frac{p(\traj)}{ p(\revtraj)}=\frac{1}{2}
\sum_{\traj} [p(\traj)- p(\revtraj)]\ln \frac{p(\traj)}{ p(\revtraj)}.
\end{align*}
For continuous-state systems, sums should be replaced by integrals. 
Using the inequality $(a-b)\ln(a/b)\ge 2(a-b)^2/(a+b)$ for nonnegative $a$ and $b$, we get the quadratic bound
\begin{align}
\ep\ge \sum_{\traj}\frac{(p(\traj)-p(\revtraj))^{2}}{p(\traj)+p(\revtraj)}\,.% = \sum_{\traj}\frac{(p(\traj)-p(\revtraj))^{2}}{2\mu(\traj)}\,.
\label{eq:pseudoEP}
\end{align}
Next, for convenience, we define  the symmetrized distribution  $\mu(\traj)=[p(\traj)+p(\revtraj)]/2=[p(\traj)+\tilde{p}(\traj)]/2$ and the function  
