where $\{(a_{ik},b_{ik})\}_{1\le i\le N}$, $1\le k\le m$, denotes the image-caption pairs for the $k$th batch of training dataset, $f_{x_I}$ and $f_{x_T}$ are the image and text encoders, respectively, and $\tau>0$ is a temperature parameter. Here, we consider problem \eqref{multi-modal} on three real text-image datasets, Flickr \cite{plummer2015flickr30k}, MSCOCO \cite{lin2014microsoft}, and CC3M \cite{sharma2018conceptual}, and choose the network structure for image encoder $f_{x_I}$ and text encoder $f_{x_T}$ as ResNet50 \cite{he2016deep} and DistilBERT \cite{sanh2019distilbert}, respectively.  

