\centerline{\includegraphics[width=0.45\textwidth]{Jmax.png}}
\caption{{Schematic diagram of the grid refinement in 2D. Each square is a block containing a number of grid points ($B_s$, not shown for readability). The grid is generated from a single initial block. When $J_\mathrm{max}$ is incremented by one, each block can be refined to four (in 3D eight) new blocks, if the wavelet criterion detects that this block is to be refined. Blocks that need no refinement are kept coarsened where possible, the example shows two blocks on $J=1$ that are not refined when incrementing $J_\mathrm{max}$.}}
