    In this subsection, we will discuss the identifiability of the meta states from the environment.
    We first introduce the concept of \textit{swap-label equivalence} between two mappings.


    \begin{definition}[Swap-Label Equivalence]
        Two mappings $C_1: \mathcal{X}\to U_1$ and $C_2: \mathcal{X}\to U_2$ are swap-label equivalent if there exists a permutation $g: U_1\to U_2$ such that $C_2(x)=g(C_1(x)), \forall x\in \mathcal{X}$.
    \end{definition}
    The definition indicates that if we can identify the meta states up to an permutation transformation, we say that the meta states are identifiable up to label swapping.
