\abstract{An $\CaA$-semigroup is a numerical semigroup without consecutive small elements. This work generalizes this concept to finite-complement submonoids of an affine cone $\CaC$. We develop algorithmic procedures to compute all $\CaA$-semigroups with a given Frobenius element (denoted by $\CaA(f)$), and with fixed Frobenius element and multiplicity. Moreover, we analyze the $\CaA(f)$-systems of generators.
Furthermore, we study $\CaA$-numerical semigroups with maximal embedding dimension, fixed Frobenius number and multiplicity, providing an algorithm for their computation and a graphical classification.
}


