\subsection{Homotopy limits via path objects}
Fix a model category $\mc M$ in which all projections are fibrations. For each $x\in \ob(\mc M)$, we fix a path object $P(x)$ with the canonical map $P(x)\overset{\pi_{1}\times \pi_{2}}\lr  x\times x$.

The \textbfit{subdivision} of a quiver $Q$ is the quiver $\olin Q\coloneqq Q(U(Q))$. Pictorially, each arrow $s\overset{e}\lr t$ in $Q$ changes in $\olin Q$ to $s\overset{(s,e)}\lr e\overset{(t,e)}\longleftarrow t$. We also use the notation $e_{v}\coloneqq (v,e)$. In particular, if $Q=Q(G)$ is graphic, $\olin Q$ is a double subdivision. Starting in $G$, then $Q$, and then $\olin Q$, we have the local progression of an edge $e$:
% https://q.uiver.app/#
\[\begin{tikzcd}
	v & w & \rightsquigarrow & {v} & e & {w} & \rightsquigarrow & {v} & {e_{v}} & e & {e_{w}} & {w}
