%   $\va{\ca I_{\ca X}(\CC)} \to \va{\ca X(\CC)}$ is the union of a trivial topological covering with the inclusion of a finite set of points, which allows one to compute the topology of $\va{\ca I_{\ca X}(\CC)}$ in terms of the topology of $\va{\ca X(\CC)}$. Possibly, one could remove these conditions by refining the techniques. 
