    Item \ref{IT:IT:0} follows from Corollary \ref{cor:coarse-map-closed}. 
        %To prove item \ref{IT:IT:0}, let $\gamma \in H(\CC)$ such that $\gamma \sigma(\gamma) = e$, and define $X_\gamma$ and $H_\gamma$ as in Section \ref{sec : twistingdefinition}. By Theorem \ref{thm:introlemme-prefere}, it suffices to show that the natural map $X_\gamma(\RR)/H_\gamma(\RR) \to (X/H)(\RR)$ is closed. Note that this map is induced by the natural map $X_\gamma \to X/H$, which induces an isomorphism $X_\gamma/H_\gamma \cong X/H$. The quotient map $X_\gamma \to X_\gamma/H_\gamma \cong X/H$ is finite, and hence $X_\gamma(\RR) \to (X/H)(\RR)$ is closed. In particular, $X_\gamma(\RR)/H_\gamma(\RR) \to (X/H)(\RR)$ is closed, proving item \ref{IT:IT:0}. 
          To prove item \ref{IT:IT:1}, note that since the action is faithful and $X$ is smooth, $f \colon \va{[X/H](\RR)} \to M(\RR)$ is surjective and closed; indeed, $f$ is closed by item \ref{IT:IT:0} and its image contains a dense open subset, so $f$ is surjective. In particular, item \ref{IT:IT:1} follows. Moreover, for $m \in C$, we have $\# f^{-1}(m) = h^1(G,m)$, see Proposition \ref{prop:fiber-H1}. Hence item \ref{IT:IT:2} follows from items \ref{IT:IT:0} and \ref{IT:IT:1}.  
