%strongest change in the quasipotential in this direction in phase space. 
Indeed, only a very small subset of all d.o.f, coinciding exactly with the variables describing the deep ocean fingerprint, shows significant variance increase prior to the AMOC collapse \cite{LOH25}. The variable that was found to exhibit the largest increase in variance is shown in Fig.~\ref{fig:veros_timeseries}a-d across the four data sets. 
In the following, we show that similar (if not better) results can be obtained with our 
the DM method which does not require prior knowledge of the edge state or a brute-force search across all d.o.f (risking false positives). Instead, only observational data close to the TP is required. 

